    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, the Austin Waves offense is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (77.82), who emerge as our premier starters. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Bailey Ober, whose 4.78 xERA and slow delivery create a prime environment for both power and potential stolen base opportunities. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** leverages a strong platoon advantage against the left-handed Patrick Sandoval, with his high-ceiling profile driving his status as a must-start. **Luis Robert Jr.** (75.65) also earns an elite designation today; his matchup against the left-handed Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez offers an ideal platoon alignment, providing a significant boost to his base projection.\n\nThe decision to bench **Nasim Nunez** (49.65) was the most difficult call of the morning. While **Nasim Nunez** possesses the elite sprint speed we value for the stolen base category, his projected batting order in the #7 slot and a difficult matchup against Shota Imanaga limited his efficiency score relative to our starters. Consequently, we opted to prioritize the high-upside profiles of **Jacob Wilson** (72.73) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (61.73), both of whom benefit from more advantageous spots in the lineup and superior platoon splits against Nick Martinez and Bryan Woo, respectively. We are also monitoring the lineup status of **Liam Hicks** (56.94) and **Drake Baldwin** (51.09); while they carry marginal scores, their projected positions ensure they remain viable, though their value is contingent on confirming their spots in the batting order.\n\nWe are entering today with a cautious eye on risk factors. While **Kyle Tucker** (71.02) remains a strong play, we are mindful of the consistency of the entire order, as most players are currently operating under \"Lineup Pending\" designations. Should **Sam Antonacci** (46.86) or **Heliot Ramos** (52.06) see their expected roles diminish once official lineups are released, we will re-evaluate our bench depth\u2014specifically **Luis Lara** and **Dominic Smith**\u2014to ensure we aren't wasting at-bats against elite situational pitchers. For now, the roster remains optimized to maximize 5x5 production, with a heavy emphasis on exploiting the soft xERA marks presented by the opposing rotation.",
